---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Benchmark from '../components/Benchmark.astro';
---
<Layout title="Forecasts meet reality" description="A public technology experiment combining TimesFM forecasting and JEV news evaluation. Explore the architecture, measured results and development of CryptoOracle.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> A PUBLIC RESEARCH NOTEBOOK</p>
        <h1>Forecasts<br /> meet <em>reality.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-intro">What happens when a time-series model meets the news — and both have to show their work?</p>
        <p class="hero-body">CryptoOracle combines crypto market data, TimesFM forecasts and JEV news evaluation in a small, measurable technology experiment.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#evidence">Explore the evidence <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/method/">Go behind the scenes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        <p class="hero-caption"><a href="https://github.com/moinsen-dev/crypto-oracle" rel="external noreferrer">Explore the source on GitHub ↗</a> · Code, tests and the research method.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-notebook" aria-labelledby="first-result">
        <div class="notebook-top"><span>FIELD NOTE / 001</span><span>17 SEP 2026</span></div>
        <div class="notebook-title"><span class="outlined-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↘</span><h2 id="first-result">The simple<br /> baseline won.</h2></div>
        <p>In the first historical experiment, keeping the last price produced less error than TimesFM.</p>
        <div class="finding-rows">
          <div><span class="coin-mark">B</span><span>Bitcoin <small>BTC</small></span><strong>+5.2%<small>model error</small></strong></div>
          <div><span class="coin-mark">E</span><span>Ethereum <small>ETH</small></span><strong>+6.1%<small>model error</small></strong></div>
          <div><span class="coin-mark">S</span><span>Solana <small>SOL</small></span><strong>+9.3%<small>model error</small></strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="notebook-bottom"><span class="mini-square" aria-hidden="true"></span><p>24-hour horizon · exploratory backtest<br /> <b>No forecasting advantage demonstrated.</b></p></div>
      </aside>
    </section>
    <div class="facts-strip" aria-label="Experiment facts">
      <div><strong>3</strong><span>assets under observation<br /> <b>BTC · ETH · SOL</b></span></div>
      <div><strong>24 / 72<span>h</span></strong><span>forecast horizons<br /> <b>Issued before evaluation</b></span></div>
      <div><strong>365</strong><span>daily historical origins<br /> <b>Per asset and horizon</b></span></div>
    </div>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="question">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE QUESTION</p><h2 id="question">Can context make<br /> a forecast more useful?</h2><p>A convincing story is easy. A useful forecast has to survive comparison, data problems and the passage of time.</p></div>
      <div class="three-columns">
        <article class="principle"><span class="index">01 / OBSERVE</span><h3>Start with the series.</h3><p>TimesFM reads 512 completed hourly closing prices. Its forecasts are stored with the model revision, inputs and issue time.</p><span class="tag">Implemented</span></article>
        <article class="principle"><span class="index">02 / UNDERSTAND</span><h3>Put news in context.</h3><p>FinBERT and JEV classify headlines. We preserve when each item became available. JEV annotations do not yet change a price forecast.</p><span class="tag">Collecting evidence</span></article>
        <article class="principle"><span class="index">03 / CHALLENGE</span><h3>Let reality answer.</h3><p>Compare forecasts with the actual outcome and simple baselines. A separate news experiment can progress when enough prospective data exists.</p><span class="tag tag-outline">Benefit still unproven</span></article>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div id="evidence" class="anchor-section"><Benchmark /></div>
    <section class="section architecture-preview" aria-labelledby="behind-scenes">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">BEHIND THE SCENES</p><h2 id="behind-scenes">A small system.<br /> <em>A visible paper trail.</em></h2><p>Models run on a dedicated research server. The public site delivers a curated, dated snapshot. Browsing this page does not contact the models or the private dashboard.</p><a class="text-link" href="/method/">Walk through the architecture <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="pipeline-preview" aria-label="Research data flow">
        <div><span>01</span><strong>Market data & news</strong><small>Source + observation time</small></div><div class="pipe-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div><span>02</span><strong>Forecasts & annotations</strong><small>Pinned inputs + model identity</small></div><div class="pipe-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div><span>03</span><strong>Journal & evaluation</strong><small>Stored prediction → later outcome</small></div><div class="pipe-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
        <div class="pipeline-public"><span>04</span><strong>This public notebook</strong><small>Selected aggregate results only</small></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="paper-teaser" aria-labelledby="paper-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">THE LIVE PAPER EXPERIMENT</p><h2 id="paper-title">$10,000.<br /> Entirely virtual.</h2><p>The virtual portfolios now record decisions, simulated trades and changing balances — with costs, data checks and a reason for every action.</p><a class="button button-light" href="/paper-portfolio/">Follow the portfolios <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="paper-stamp"><span class="pill pill-light">VIRTUAL · OBSERVING LIVE</span><p>Starting capital</p><strong>$10,000<span>USD</span></strong><div class="paper-line"></div><p>Recorded decisions.<br /> Transparent simulated results.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="closing-note"><p class="eyebrow">BUILT TO BE QUESTIONED</p><h2>The useful part is what we learn.</h2><p>Follow the decisions, the checks and the things that did not work as hoped.</p><a class="text-link" href="/build-notes/">Read the development journal <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  </div>
</Layout>
